    "features": [
      {
        "name": "Brave",
        "section": "Traits",
        "content": "<h5>Brave</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">This Creature has Advantage on Saving Throws to avoid or end the Frightened Condition.</p>",
        "rawSource": "This Creature has Advantage on Saving Throws to avoid or end the Frightened Condition."
      },
      {
        "name": "Multiattack",
        "section": "Actions",
        "content": "<h5>Multiattack</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">This Creature makes two Melee Attacks. It can replace one of them with a Grapple.</p>",
        "rawSource": "This Creature makes two Melee Attacks. It can replace one of them with a Grapple. \n"
      },
      {
        "name": "Punch",
        "section": "Actions",
        "content": "<h5>Punch</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><em>Melee Weapon Attack:</em> +8 to hit, reach 5ft., one target, <em>Hit:</em> 8 (1d6+4) Bludgeoning Damage.</p>",
        "rawSource": "*Melee Weapon Attack:* +8 to hit, reach 5ft., one target, *Hit:* 8 (1d6+4) Bludgeoning Damage."
      },
      {
        "name": "Swallow Whole",
        "section": "Bonus Actions",
        "content": "<h5>Swallow Whole</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">The Devourer chooses a Medium or smaller Creature it is currently Grappling; that Creature must succeed on a DC17 Strength Saving Throw or be swallowed by the Devourer. The Grappled Condition ends on the swallowed Creature; a swallowed Creature has the Blinded and Restrained Conditions and can't teleport, it has Total Cover against Attacks and other effects from outside of the Devourer, and it takes 21 (6d6) Acid damage at the start of each of the Devourer's Turns.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">The Devourer can only have one Creature swallowed at a time. While it has a Creature swallowed, this Creature is Resistant to Physical Damage dealt from outside of it, but its Speed is halved.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">If the Devourer takes 30 or more Damage on a single Turn from a Creature inside of it, it must succeed on a DC20 Constitution Saving Throw or spit out the swallowed Creature at the end of the Turn, which falls Prone in a space within 10 feet of the Devourer. If the Devourer dies, it immediately spits out any swallowed Creature.</p>",
        "rawSource": "The Devourer chooses a Medium or smaller Creature it is currently Grappling; that Creature must succeed on a DC17 Strength Saving Throw or be swallowed by the Devourer. The Grappled Condition ends on the swallowed Creature; a swallowed Creature has the Blinded and Restrained Conditions and can't teleport, it has Total Cover against Attacks and other effects from outside of the Devourer, and it takes 21 (6d6) Acid damage at the start of each of the Devourer's Turns.\n\nThe Devourer can only have one Creature swallowed at a time. While it has a Creature swallowed, this Creature is Resistant to Physical Damage dealt from outside of it, but its Speed is halved.\n\nIf the Devourer takes 30 or more Damage on a single Turn from a Creature inside of it, it must succeed on a DC20 Constitution Saving Throw or spit out the swallowed Creature at the end of the Turn, which falls Prone in a space within 10 feet of the Devourer. If the Devourer dies, it immediately spits out any swallowed Creature."
      }
    ],
