    "features": [
      {
        "name": "Brave",
        "section": "Traits",
        "content": "<h5>Brave</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">This Creature has Advantage on Saving Throws to avoid or end the Frightened Condition.</p>",
        "rawSource": "This Creature has Advantage on Saving Throws to avoid or end the Frightened Condition.\n"
      },
      {
        "name": "Damage Reduction",
        "section": "Traits",
        "content": "<h5>Damage Reduction</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">This Creature has 3 DR against Physical Damage.</p>",
        "rawSource": "This Creature has 3 DR against Physical Damage.\n"
      },
      {
        "name": "Ruination Remains",
        "section": "Traits",
        "content": "<h5>Ruination Remains</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">After this Creature creates any effect that forces a Creature to make a Saving Throw, a puddle of miasma is created in the same area affected by that Saving Throw until the beginning of the Annihilator's next Turn. When a Creature enters the Miasma, they take 9 (2d8) Necrotic Damage.</p>",
        "rawSource": "After this Creature creates any effect that forces a Creature to make a Saving Throw, a puddle of miasma is created in the same area affected by that Saving Throw until the beginning of the Annihilator's next Turn. When a Creature enters the Miasma, they take 9 (2d8) Necrotic Damage. \n"
      },
      {
        "name": "Siege Attacker",
        "section": "Traits",
        "content": "<h5>Siege Attacker</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">This Creature does double Damage to Vehicles and Structures.</p>",
        "rawSource": "This Creature does double Damage to Vehicles and Structures.\n"
      },
      {
        "name": "Touch of The Sanguinarch",
        "section": "Traits",
        "content": "<h5>Touch of The Sanguinarch</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">When this Creature would be killed in a way that would not destroy their body, they do not immediately die. Instead, they die at the end of their next Turn; during this time, they are immune to all Conditions and effects that would not destroy their body.</p>",
        "rawSource": "When this Creature would be killed in a way that would not destroy their body, they do not immediately die. Instead, they die at the end of their next Turn; during this time, they are immune to all Conditions and effects that would not destroy their body.\n\n\\column"
      },
      {
        "name": "Multiattack",
        "section": "Actions",
        "content": "<h5>Multiattack</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">This Creature makes two Attacks with its Stickybomb Mortar or three with Slam.</p>",
        "rawSource": "This Creature makes two Attacks with its Stickybomb Mortar or three with Slam.\n"
      },
      {
        "name": "Indiscriminate Bombardment (Recharge 4+)",
        "section": "Actions",
        "content": "<h5>Indiscriminate Bombardment (Recharge 4+)</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">The Annihilator chooses a location within 100 feet and fires four explosives at it. Roll four pairs of dice; a d12 and a d4, respectively. For each pair, the number rolled on the d12 determines the direction one of the four bombs scatters in, as if it were a clock face with the Annihilator in the \"six o'clock\" direction. The number rolled on the d4 is the distance that bomb scatters; multiply the number rolled by ten.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">After determining the four locations, each Creature in a 10-foot-radius of any of those points must make a DC 14 Dexterity Saving Throw. On a failed Save, they take 18 (4d8) Thunder Damage; on a successful Save, they take half as much.</p>",
        "rawSource": "The Annihilator chooses a location within 100 feet and fires four explosives at it. Roll four pairs of dice; a d12 and a d4, respectively. For each pair, the number rolled on the d12 determines the direction one of the four bombs scatters in, as if it were a clock face with the Annihilator in the \"six o'clock\" direction. The number rolled on the d4 is the distance that bomb scatters; multiply the number rolled by ten. \n\nAfter determining the four locations, each Creature in a 10-foot-radius of any of those points must make a DC 14 Dexterity Saving Throw. On a failed Save, they take 18 (4d8) Thunder Damage; on a successful Save, they take half as much.\n"
      },
      {
        "name": "Slam",
        "section": "Actions",
        "content": "<h5>Slam</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><em>Melee Weapon Attack:</em> +5 to hit, reach 5ft., one target, <em>Hit:</em> 20 (4d8+2) Bludgeoning Damage</p>",
        "rawSource": "*Melee Weapon Attack:* +5 to hit, reach 5ft., one target, *Hit:* 20 (4d8+2) Bludgeoning Damage\n"
      },
      {
        "name": "Stickybomb Mortar",
        "section": "Actions",
        "content": "<h5>Stickybomb Mortar</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><em>Ranged Weapon Attack:</em> +5 to hit, range 100 ft., one target, <em>Hit:</em> If the target is a Creature, the Stickybomb sticks to them. At the beginning of this Creature's next Turn, all of their fired Stickybombs explode; all Creatures within a 10-foot-radius sphere centred on each Stickybomb must make a DC 14 Dexterity Saving Throw. On a failed Save, they take 18 (4d8) Thunder Damage, or half as much (9) on a successful Save. If the Stickybomb is stuck to a Creature, that Creature automatically fails this Saving Throw.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">This Attack does not require line of sight, but there can be no roof obstructing the arc of the stickybomb.</p>",
        "rawSource": "*Ranged Weapon Attack:* +5 to hit, range 100 ft., one target, *Hit:* If the target is a Creature, the Stickybomb sticks to them. At the beginning of this Creature's next Turn, all of their fired Stickybombs explode; all Creatures within a 10-foot-radius sphere centred on each Stickybomb must make a DC 14 Dexterity Saving Throw. On a failed Save, they take 18 (4d8) Thunder Damage, or half as much (9) on a successful Save. If the Stickybomb is stuck to a Creature, that Creature automatically fails this Saving Throw.\n\nThis Attack does not require line of sight, but there can be no roof obstructing the arc of the stickybomb.\n"
      }
    ],
